-- allium: 3
-- organizations.allium — organizations, their teams, team membership, invitations and team repository access.
--
-- Scope: Everything that makes an organization a shared owner of repositories:
--   the organization's lifecycle and settings, its membership (always mediated
--   by teams), the Owners team and its invariants, teams with their access
--   level and per-unit grants, team invitations, the set of repositories each
--   team covers, membership visibility, org-level blocking and the org profile.
--
-- Includes:
--   - Organization create (who may, instance switches), profile settings,
--     rename, visibility (public/limited/private), avatar, delete (refused
--     while it still owns repositories or packages), purge on behalf of the
--     system (owner account deletion, moderation).
--   - OrgMembership (public/concealed), leaving, removal by owners.
--   - Team create/edit/delete, access mode (read/write/admin/owner), per-unit
--     access, includes-all-repositories, can-create-org-repo.
--   - The Owners team: exists from creation, cannot be deleted or renamed,
--     always owner access over all repositories, never empties.
--   - TeamMembership add/remove/join/leave, provenance (creator, co-opted by a
--     person, synchronised from an authentication source).
--   - TeamInvite by account or by e-mail address, expiry, accept/decline/revoke,
--     ADD_MEMBERS_BY_INVITATIONS consent flow.
--   - TeamRepository add/remove/add-all/remove-all, including from the
--     repository side by repository admins when the org allows it.
--   - Who can see the organization, its members and its teams.
--   - Organization profile from the `.profile` repository.
--
-- Excludes:
--   - Org-level labels (owned by issues.allium).
--   - Org webhooks (webhooks.allium), org actions secrets/variables/runners
--     (actions.allium), org packages and cleanup rules (packages.allium), org
--     projects (projects.allium), org OAuth2 applications (authentication.allium),
--     org quota (quota.allium).
--   - The derived repository permission a team grants: computed by
--     access.allium from Team, TeamUnitAccess and TeamRepository declared here.
--   - Org dashboards, org activity feeds (notifications.allium); explore page and
--     org search (discovery.allium).
--   - "Ghost team" placeholder and the doctor repair of inconsistent Owners-team
--     units: legacy data-repair, not behaviour a rebuild needs.
--   - Membership reason "unknown": exists only for rows created before
--     provenance was tracked (legacy).
--   - The deprecated API `units` list (replaced by a per-unit map): Gitea
--     API compatibility only.
--   - Denormalised counters (num_members, num_teams, num_repos): derived here as
--     `.count` of relationships.
--   - Org-level user blocking (OrganizationBlocksUser / OrganizationUnblocksUser,
--     the OrganizationBlockList surface): owned by accounts.allium, which
--     owns UserBlock with an organization blocker; it uses is_org_owner from
--     here. Note: a block does not end an existing org membership.
--   - Team-scoped review requests are removed with a team: pulls.allium reacts
--     to TeamDeleted.
--
-- Emits (domain triggers other modules react to):
--   OrganizationCreated(organization, creator)
--   OrganizationRenamed(organization, old_name, new_name)
--   OrganizationVisibilityChanged(organization)
--   OrganizationProfileUpdated(organization)
--   OrganizationAvatarChanged(organization)
--   OrganizationDeleted(organization)
--   OrganizationPurgeStarted(organization)
--   OrgMemberAdded(organization, user)
--   OrgMemberRemoved(organization, user)
--   OrgMembershipVisibilityChanged(membership)
--   TeamCreated(team, actor)
--   TeamUpdated(team, actor)
--   TeamAccessChanged(team)
--   TeamDeleted(team)
--   TeamMemberAdded(team, user)
--   TeamMemberRemoved(team, user)
--   TeamInviteCreated(invite, inviter)   -- notifications mails the invitee
--   TeamInviteDeclined(invite)
--   TeamRepositoryAdded(team, repository)
--   TeamRepositoryRemoved(team, repository)
--
-- Reacts to:
--   repositories/Repository.created  -- add new org repo to includes-all teams
--   OrgRepositoryArrived(repository) / OrgRepositoryDeparted(repository, organization)
--       (see REQUESTs: emitted by repositories on transfer/delete)
--   authentication/ExternalGroupsAsserted(user, source, groups)  -- group-to-team sync
--   authentication/AuthSourceDeleted(source)                      -- forget provenance
--   accounts/UserPurged(user)  -- leave every org; purge orgs where last owner
--   administration/OrganizationCreatedForUserByAdmin(admin, user, name, visibility)  -- found it
--   moderation/ModeratorDeletesOrganization(admin, organization)  -- purge the org

use "./accounts.allium" as accounts
use "./access.allium" as access
use "./repositories.allium" as repositories
use "./authentication.allium" as authentication
use "./moderation.allium" as moderation
use "./administration.allium" as administration

------------------------------------------------------------
-- Enumerations
------------------------------------------------------------

-- How a person came to be on a team.
-- from: models/organization/team_user.go:20
enum MembershipReason {
    org_creator | added_by_user | added_by_auth_source
}

------------------------------------------------------------
-- Entities and Variants
------------------------------------------------------------

-- An account that owns repositories on behalf of a group of people. Shares the
-- owner namespace with accounts/User (one name cannot be both).
-- from: models/organization/org.go:84
entity Organization {
    name: String                              -- unique across users and orgs, max 40, renamable
    full_name: String?                        -- max 100
    description: String?                      -- max 255, rendered as markdown on the profile
    website: String?                          -- max 255, must be a valid site URL
    location: String?                         -- max 50
    email: String?                            -- public contact address, max 255
    visibility: accounts/Visibility
    repo_admin_change_team_access: Boolean    -- repo admins may add/remove teams on their repo
    max_repo_creation: Integer?               -- null: instance default limit applies (site admin only)
    has_custom_avatar: Boolean
    created_at: Timestamp

    -- Relationships
    teams: Team with organization = this
    memberships: OrgMembership with organization = this
    invites: TeamInvite with organization = this

    -- Projections
    members: memberships -> user
    public_members: memberships where is_public = true -> user
    owners_team: Team with organization = this and is_owners_team = true
    owners: owners_team.members

    -- Derived
    is_public: visibility = public
    member_count: memberships.count
    team_count: teams.count
    owner_count: owners.count

    has_member(u): u in members
    has_owner(u): u in owners
    -- Owner, or member of any team with admin access.
    has_admin(u): teams.any(t => t.is_admin_team and u in t.members)
    -- May create repositories owned by the org.
    lets_create_repo(u): u.is_admin or teams.any(t => (t.can_create_org_repo or t.access_mode = owner) and u in t.members)
    -- Sees every team (not only the ones they are on).
    sees_all_teams(u): u.is_admin or u in owners
        or teams.any(t => t.includes_all_repositories and t.access_mode in {admin, owner} and u in t.members)
    -- Which signed-in people can see that the organization exists at all.
    -- from: models/organization/org.go:526
    is_visible_to(u): u.is_admin or u in members
        or (not u.is_restricted and visibility in {public, limited})
    -- Signed-in people for whom concealed memberships are listed too.
    sees_concealed_members(u): u.is_admin or u in members
}

-- The fact that a person belongs to an organization. Exists exactly while the
-- person is on at least one of the organization's teams.
-- from: models/organization/org_user.go:21
entity OrgMembership {
    organization: Organization
    user: accounts/User
    is_public: Boolean                        -- shown on the org and the user's profile to everyone
    joined_at: Timestamp

    team_memberships: TeamMembership with organization = organization and user = user
}

-- A named group within an organization granting its members one access level
-- over a set of the organization's repositories.
-- from: models/organization/team.go:66
entity Team {
    organization: Organization
    name: String                              -- AlphaDashDot, max 255, unique per org ignoring case, not "new"
    description: String?                      -- max 255
    access_mode: access/AccessMode            -- read | write (summary of unit grants) | admin | owner
    includes_all_repositories: Boolean        -- covers every current and future org repository
    can_create_org_repo: Boolean
    is_owners_team: Boolean

    -- Relationships
    memberships: TeamMembership with team = this
    unit_accesses: TeamUnitAccess with team = this
    repository_links: TeamRepository with team = this
    invites: TeamInvite with team = this

    -- Projections
    members: memberships -> user
    repositories: repository_links -> repository
    pending_invites: invites where status = pending
    expired_invites: invites where status = expired

    -- Derived
    member_count: memberships.count
    repository_count: repository_links.count
    is_admin_team: access_mode in {admin, owner}
    has_member(u): u in members
    covers(r): r in repositories
    -- Who may open the team page and list its members and repositories.
    -- from: services/context/org.go:245
    can_be_viewed_by(u): u in members or organization.sees_all_teams(u)
}

-- One person's place on one team.
-- from: models/organization/team_user.go:36
entity TeamMembership {
    team: Team
    organization: Organization                -- always team.organization
    user: accounts/User
    reason: MembershipReason
    added_by: accounts/User?                  -- set when reason = added_by_user
    auth_source: authentication/AuthSource?   -- set when reason = added_by_auth_source
    added_at: Timestamp
}

-- The access a team grants to one repository unit. Admin and owner teams carry
-- their own mode on every unit, except external wiki/tracker which are read.
-- Read/write teams grant at most write per unit.
-- from: models/organization/team_unit.go:15
entity TeamUnitAccess {
    team: Team
    unit: repositories/UnitKind
    access_mode: access/AccessMode
}

-- A repository a team covers. The repository is always owned by the team's org.
-- from: models/organization/team_repo.go:17
entity TeamRepository {
    team: Team
    repository: repositories/Repository
}

-- A pending offer to join a team, addressed either to an existing account or to
-- an e-mail address. Accepting it is the invitee's consent to join the org.
-- from: models/organization/team_invite.go:97
entity TeamInvite {
    team: Team
    organization: Organization                -- always team.organization
    inviter: accounts/User
    email: String
    invited_user: accounts/User?              -- null: invitation by e-mail address only
    token: String                             -- unguessable secret carried by the invite link
    created_at: Timestamp
    expires_at: Timestamp?                    -- null: never expires (expiry disabled)
    status: pending | expired

    transitions status {
        pending -> expired
        terminal: expired
    }

    is_addressed_to(u): invited_user = null or invited_user = u
}

------------------------------------------------------------
-- Config
------------------------------------------------------------

config {
    -- [admin] DISABLE_REGULAR_ORG_CREATION: only site admins may create orgs.
    -- This module owns it; accounts and administration read
    -- organizations/config.disable_regular_org_creation.
    disable_regular_org_creation: Boolean = false
    -- [service] DEFAULT_ORG_VISIBILITY: preselected visibility on the create form.
    default_org_visibility: accounts/Visibility = public
    -- [service] DEFAULT_ORG_MEMBER_VISIBLE: new memberships start public.
    default_org_member_visible: Boolean = false
    -- [service] ADD_MEMBERS_BY_INVITATIONS: adding someone who is not yet an org
    -- member sends an invitation instead of adding them directly.
    add_members_by_invitations: Boolean = false
    -- [service] TEAM_INVITATION_EXPIRY_DAYS: zero disables expiry.
    team_invitation_expiry: Duration = 14.days
    -- Organization name length limit (shared with user names).
    max_org_name_length: Integer = 40
    max_full_name_length: Integer = 100
    max_description_length: Integer = 255
    max_website_length: Integer = 255
    max_location_length: Integer = 50
    max_team_name_length: Integer = 255
    max_team_description_length: Integer = 255
}

------------------------------------------------------------
-- Rules: creating an organization
------------------------------------------------------------

-- A signed-in person founds an organization and becomes its first owner.
-- from: models/organization/org.go:268
rule UserCreatesOrganization {
    when: UserCreatesOrganization(creator, name, visibility, repo_admin_change_team_access)

    requires: creator.is_admin
        or (creator.allow_create_organization and not config.disable_regular_org_creation)
    requires: is_usable_owner_name(name)
    requires: length(name) <= config.max_org_name_length
    requires: owner_name_available(name)

    ensures:
        let org = Organization.created(
            name: name,
            visibility: visibility,
            repo_admin_change_team_access: repo_admin_change_team_access,
            has_custom_avatar: false,
            created_at: now
        )
        let owners = Team.created(
            organization: org,
            name: "Owners",
            access_mode: owner,
            includes_all_repositories: true,
            can_create_org_repo: true,
            is_owners_team: true
        )
        -- every unit at owner; the external wiki and tracker at read
        TeamUnitAccess.created(team: owners, unit: code, access_mode: owner)
        TeamUnitAccess.created(team: owners, unit: issues, access_mode: owner)
        TeamUnitAccess.created(team: owners, unit: pull_requests, access_mode: owner)
        TeamUnitAccess.created(team: owners, unit: releases, access_mode: owner)
        TeamUnitAccess.created(team: owners, unit: wiki, access_mode: owner)
        TeamUnitAccess.created(team: owners, unit: external_wiki, access_mode: read)
        TeamUnitAccess.created(team: owners, unit: external_tracker, access_mode: read)
        TeamUnitAccess.created(team: owners, unit: projects, access_mode: owner)
        TeamUnitAccess.created(team: owners, unit: packages, access_mode: owner)
        TeamUnitAccess.created(team: owners, unit: actions, access_mode: owner)
        OrgMembership.created(
            organization: org,
            user: creator,
            is_public: config.default_org_member_visible,
            joined_at: now
        )
        TeamMembership.created(
            team: owners,
            organization: org,
            user: creator,
            reason: org_creator,
            added_at: now
        )
        OrganizationCreated(organization: org, creator: creator)

    @guidance
        -- Web: GET/POST /org/create. API: POST /orgs.
        -- The name check covers reserved names and patterns and the
        -- character set accepted for user names; a name held by any
        -- user or organization is taken. A stale rename redirect for the
        -- name is dropped (accounts reacts to OrganizationCreated).
        -- A generated identicon is the initial avatar.
}

-- A site admin founds an organization on behalf of an existing person, who
-- becomes its first owner. administration owns the admin entry point
-- (AdminCreatesOrganizationForUser) and its admin check; this module owns the
-- creation.
-- from: routers/api/v1/admin/org.go:24
rule CreateOrganizationForUserByAdmin {
    when: administration/OrganizationCreatedForUserByAdmin(admin, user, name, visibility)

    let owner = user
    requires: owner.kind in {individual, bot}
    requires: owner.is_admin
        or (owner.allow_create_organization and not config.disable_regular_org_creation)
    requires: is_usable_owner_name(name)
    requires: length(name) <= config.max_org_name_length
    requires: owner_name_available(name)

    ensures:
        let org = Organization.created(
            name: name,
            visibility: visibility,
            repo_admin_change_team_access: false,
            has_custom_avatar: false,
            created_at: now
        )
        let owners = Team.created(
            organization: org,
            name: "Owners",
            access_mode: owner,
            includes_all_repositories: true,
            can_create_org_repo: true,
            is_owners_team: true
        )
        -- every unit at owner; the external wiki and tracker at read
        TeamUnitAccess.created(team: owners, unit: code, access_mode: owner)
        TeamUnitAccess.created(team: owners, unit: issues, access_mode: owner)
        TeamUnitAccess.created(team: owners, unit: pull_requests, access_mode: owner)
        TeamUnitAccess.created(team: owners, unit: releases, access_mode: owner)
        TeamUnitAccess.created(team: owners, unit: wiki, access_mode: owner)
        TeamUnitAccess.created(team: owners, unit: external_wiki, access_mode: read)
        TeamUnitAccess.created(team: owners, unit: external_tracker, access_mode: read)
        TeamUnitAccess.created(team: owners, unit: projects, access_mode: owner)
        TeamUnitAccess.created(team: owners, unit: packages, access_mode: owner)
        TeamUnitAccess.created(team: owners, unit: actions, access_mode: owner)
        OrgMembership.created(
            organization: org,
            user: owner,
            is_public: config.default_org_member_visible,
            joined_at: now
        )
        TeamMembership.created(
            team: owners,
            organization: org,
            user: owner,
            reason: org_creator,
            added_at: now
        )
        OrganizationCreated(organization: org, creator: owner)

    @guidance
        -- API: POST /admin/users/{username}/orgs.
}

------------------------------------------------------------
-- Rules: organization settings
------------------------------------------------------------

-- from: routers/web/org/setting.go:120
rule OwnerUpdatesOrganizationProfile {
    when: OwnerUpdatesOrganizationProfile(actor, org, full_name, description, website, location, email)

    requires: is_org_owner(org, actor) or actor.is_admin
    requires: full_name = null or length(full_name) <= config.max_full_name_length
    requires: description = null or length(description) <= config.max_description_length
    requires: website = null or (is_valid_site_url(website) and length(website) <= config.max_website_length)
    requires: location = null or length(location) <= config.max_location_length
    requires: email = null or is_valid_email(email)

    ensures: org.full_name = full_name
    ensures: org.description = description
    ensures: org.website = website
    ensures: org.location = location
    ensures: org.email = email
    ensures: OrganizationProfileUpdated(organization: org)

    @guidance
        -- Web: POST /org/{org}/settings. API: PATCH /orgs/{org} (each field
        -- optional; an empty e-mail clears it).
}

-- from: routers/web/org/setting.go:135
rule OwnerChangesOrganizationVisibility {
    when: OwnerChangesOrganizationVisibility(actor, org, visibility)

    requires: is_org_owner(org, actor) or actor.is_admin
    requires: visibility != org.visibility

    ensures: org.visibility = visibility
    ensures: OrganizationVisibilityChanged(organization: org)

    @guidance
        -- Part of the settings form / PATCH /orgs/{org}. Unlike user
        -- accounts, organizations are not restricted by the instance's
        -- allowed-user-visibility list. Search indexes of the org's
        -- repositories are refreshed (discovery reacts).
}

-- Whether repository admins may grant or withdraw team access on their repo.
-- from: routers/web/org/setting.go:128
rule OwnerSetsRepoAdminTeamAccess {
    when: OwnerSetsRepoAdminTeamAccess(actor, org, allowed)

    requires: is_org_owner(org, actor) or actor.is_admin

    ensures: org.repo_admin_change_team_access = allowed
}

-- from: routers/web/org/setting.go:130
rule AdminSetsOrganizationRepoLimit {
    when: AdminSetsOrganizationRepoLimit(admin, org, limit)

    requires: admin.is_admin

    ensures: org.max_repo_creation = limit

    @guidance
        -- null restores the instance default (repositories' MAX_CREATION_LIMIT).
}

-- from: services/user/user.go:69
rule OwnerRenamesOrganization {
    when: OwnerRenamesOrganization(actor, org, new_name)

    requires: is_org_owner(org, actor) or actor.is_admin
    requires: new_name != org.name
    requires: is_usable_owner_name(new_name)
    requires: length(new_name) <= config.max_org_name_length
    requires: owner_name_available(new_name) or lower(new_name) = lower(org.name)
    requires: owner_name_claimable(new_name, org) or actor.is_admin

    let old_name = org.name

    ensures: org.name = new_name
    ensures: OrganizationRenamed(organization: org, old_name: old_name, new_name: new_name)

    @guidance
        -- Web: name field of POST /org/{org}/settings. API: POST
        -- /orgs/{org}/rename. Organizations can always be renamed (no
        -- local-account restriction). The name cooldown (accounts'
        -- USERNAME_COOLDOWN_PERIOD) applies unless a site admin renames.
        -- A pure change of letter case is always allowed. accounts records a
        -- redirect from the old name; repositories update owner names.
}

-- from: routers/web/org/setting.go:162
rule OwnerUploadsOrganizationAvatar {
    when: OwnerUploadsOrganizationAvatar(actor, org, image)

    requires: is_org_owner(org, actor) or actor.is_admin
    requires: is_acceptable_avatar(image)

    ensures: org.has_custom_avatar = true
    ensures: OrganizationAvatarChanged(organization: org)

    @guidance
        -- Web: POST /org/{org}/settings/avatar. API: POST /orgs/{org}/avatar
        -- (base64 image). Size and dimension limits are accounts' avatar
        -- settings ([avatar] MAX_FILE_SIZE, MAX_WIDTH, MAX_HEIGHT).
}

-- from: routers/web/org/setting.go:174
rule OwnerDeletesOrganizationAvatar {
    when: OwnerDeletesOrganizationAvatar(actor, org)

    requires: is_org_owner(org, actor) or actor.is_admin

    ensures: org.has_custom_avatar = false
    ensures: OrganizationAvatarChanged(organization: org)

    @guidance
        -- Web: POST /org/{org}/settings/avatar/delete. API: DELETE /orgs/{org}/avatar.
        -- Falls back to a generated identicon.
}

------------------------------------------------------------
-- Rules: deleting an organization
------------------------------------------------------------

-- An owner deletes an empty organization. Refused while it owns repositories
-- or packages: those must be deleted or transferred first.
-- from: services/org/org.go:22
rule OwnerDeletesOrganization {
    when: OwnerDeletesOrganization(actor, org, confirmation_name)

    requires: is_org_owner(org, actor) or actor.is_admin
    requires: confirmation_name = org.name
    requires: owned_repository_count(org) = 0
    requires: owned_package_count(org) = 0

    ensures:
        for i in org.invites:
            not exists i
        for t in org.teams:
            for tm in t.memberships:
                not exists tm
            for tu in t.unit_accesses:
                not exists tu
            for tr in t.repository_links:
                not exists tr
            not exists t
        for m in org.memberships:
            not exists m
        not exists org
        OrganizationDeleted(organization: org)

    @guidance
        -- Web: POST /org/{org}/settings/delete (must type the org name).
        -- API: DELETE /orgs/{org}. Reactors to OrganizationDeleted remove the
        -- org's actions secrets, runners and registration tokens (actions),
        -- its follows, blocks and uploaded avatar (accounts), its webhooks,
        -- labels and projects. The name becomes free immediately.
}

-- The system deletes an organization together with everything it owns: when
-- its last owner's account is purged, or by moderation.
-- from: services/org/org.go:23
rule SystemPurgesOrganization {
    when: OrganizationPurgeRequested(organization)

    ensures:
        for i in organization.invites:
            not exists i
        for t in organization.teams:
            for tm in t.memberships:
                not exists tm
            for tu in t.unit_accesses:
                not exists tu
            for tr in t.repository_links:
                not exists tr
            not exists t
        for m in organization.memberships:
            not exists m
        not exists organization
        OrganizationPurgeStarted(organization: organization)
        OrganizationDeleted(organization: organization)

    @guidance
        -- repositories and packages react to OrganizationPurgeStarted by
        -- deleting every repository and package the organization owns before the organization
        -- record goes. Triggered by accounts (purging a user who is last
        -- owner) and moderation (admin acting on an abuse report).
}

-- A site admin deletes an organization in response to an abuse report.
-- from: routers/web/admin/reports.go:329
rule ModeratorPurgesOrganization {
    when: moderation/ModeratorDeletesOrganization(admin, organization)

    ensures: OrganizationPurgeRequested(organization: organization)
}

------------------------------------------------------------
-- Rules: organization membership
------------------------------------------------------------

-- A member shows or hides their own membership; owners may change it for any
-- member.
-- from: routers/web/org/members.go:93
rule MemberChangesMembershipVisibility {
    when: MemberChangesMembershipVisibility(actor, org, membership, is_public)

    requires: membership.organization = org
    requires: actor = membership.user
        or is_org_owner(membership.organization, actor)
        or actor.is_admin
    requires: membership.is_public != is_public

    ensures: membership.is_public = is_public
    ensures: OrgMembershipVisibilityChanged(membership: membership)

    @guidance
        -- Web: POST /org/{org}/members/action/{public|private}?uid=
        -- (self or owner). API: PUT/DELETE /orgs/{org}/public_members/{username}
        -- (self only — see open question).
}

-- A member leaves the organization, which takes them off every team.
-- from: models/org.go:18
rule MemberLeavesOrganization {
    when: MemberLeavesOrganization(user, org)

    let membership = OrgMembership{organization: org, user: user}

    requires: exists membership
    requires: not is_org_owner(org, user) or owner_count(org) > 1

    ensures:
        for tm in membership.team_memberships:
            not exists tm
            TeamMemberRemoved(team: tm.team, user: user)
        not exists membership
        OrgMemberRemoved(organization: org, user: user)

    @guidance
        -- Web: POST /org/{org}/members/action/leave, also offered from
        -- /user/settings/organization. The last owner cannot leave.
}

-- An owner removes a person from the organization (every team).
-- from: routers/web/org/members.go:106
rule OwnerRemovesOrgMember {
    when: OwnerRemovesOrgMember(actor, org, user)

    let membership = OrgMembership{organization: org, user: user}

    requires: is_org_owner(org, actor) or actor.is_admin
    requires: exists membership
    requires: not is_org_owner(org, user) or owner_count(org) > 1

    ensures:
        for tm in membership.team_memberships:
            not exists tm
            TeamMemberRemoved(team: tm.team, user: user)
        not exists membership
        OrgMemberRemoved(organization: org, user: user)

    @guidance
        -- Web: POST /org/{org}/members/action/remove?uid=.
        -- API: DELETE /orgs/{org}/members/{username}.
}

-- An owner brings an existing person into the organization by putting them on
-- one or more teams. Under ADD_MEMBERS_BY_INVITATIONS each team gets an
-- invitation instead (see OwnerAddsTeamMember).
-- from: routers/web/org/members.go:113
rule OwnerAddsMemberToOrganization {
    when: OwnerAddsMemberToOrganization(actor, org, user, teams)

    requires: is_org_owner(org, actor) or actor.is_admin
    requires: user.kind in {individual, bot, remote}
    requires: not is_org_member(org, user)
    requires: not config.add_members_by_invitations
        or not has_pending_org_invite(org, user)
    requires: teams.count > 0
    requires: teams.all(t => t.organization = org)

    ensures:
        for t in teams:
            OwnerAddsTeamMember(actor: actor, team: t, user: user)

    @guidance
        -- Web: POST /org/{org}/members/action/add with uname and team_<id>
        -- checkboxes. Organizations cannot be members.
}

-- A person whose account is being purged is taken out of every organization;
-- organizations where they are the last owner are purged with them. (A
-- non-purge account deletion is refused by accounts while the person still
-- belongs to any organization.)
-- from: services/user/user.go:244
rule RemoveDeletedUserFromOrganizations {
    when: accounts/UserPurged(user)

    ensures:
        for m in OrgMemberships where user = user:
            if is_org_owner(m.organization, user) and owner_count(m.organization) = 1:
                OrganizationPurgeRequested(organization: m.organization)
            else:
                for tm in m.team_memberships:
                    not exists tm
                    TeamMemberRemoved(team: tm.team, user: user)
                not exists m
                OrgMemberRemoved(organization: m.organization, user: user)
}

-- Losing the last team means losing the organization.
-- from: models/org_team.go:519
rule DropOrgMembershipWithoutTeams {
    when: TeamMemberRemoved(team, user)

    let membership = OrgMembership{organization: team.organization, user: user}

    requires: exists membership
    requires: not exists TeamMembership{organization: team.organization, user: user}

    ensures: not exists membership
    ensures: OrgMemberRemoved(organization: team.organization, user: user)

    @guidance
        -- Removing someone from their last team (or deleting their last
        -- team) ends their organization membership. access, repositories
        -- and issues react to OrgMemberRemoved / TeamMemberRemoved by
        -- dropping watches, issue subscriptions and assignments on
        -- repositories the person can no longer read.
}

------------------------------------------------------------
-- Rules: teams
------------------------------------------------------------

-- from: models/org_team.go:177
rule OwnerCreatesTeam {
    when: OwnerCreatesTeam(actor, org, name, description, access_mode, grants, includes_all_repositories, can_create_org_repo)

    requires: is_org_owner(org, actor) or actor.is_admin
    requires: is_alpha_dash_dot(name)
    requires: length(name) <= config.max_team_name_length
    requires: lower(name) != "new"
    requires: not team_name_taken(org, name)
    requires: description = null or length(description) <= config.max_team_description_length
    requires: access_mode in {read, write, admin}
    requires: access_mode = admin or grants_some_unit(grants)

    let effective_mode = team_mode_for(access_mode, grants)

    ensures:
        let team = Team.created(
            organization: org,
            name: name,
            description: description,
            access_mode: effective_mode,
            includes_all_repositories: includes_all_repositories,
            can_create_org_repo: can_create_org_repo,
            is_owners_team: false
        )
        if access_mode = admin:
            -- every unit at admin; the external wiki and tracker at read
            TeamUnitAccess.created(team: team, unit: code, access_mode: admin)
            TeamUnitAccess.created(team: team, unit: issues, access_mode: admin)
            TeamUnitAccess.created(team: team, unit: pull_requests, access_mode: admin)
            TeamUnitAccess.created(team: team, unit: releases, access_mode: admin)
            TeamUnitAccess.created(team: team, unit: wiki, access_mode: admin)
            TeamUnitAccess.created(team: team, unit: external_wiki, access_mode: read)
            TeamUnitAccess.created(team: team, unit: external_tracker, access_mode: read)
            TeamUnitAccess.created(team: team, unit: projects, access_mode: admin)
            TeamUnitAccess.created(team: team, unit: packages, access_mode: admin)
            TeamUnitAccess.created(team: team, unit: actions, access_mode: admin)
        else:
            for g in grants:
                if g.unit in {external_wiki, external_tracker}:
                    if g.access_mode != none:
                        TeamUnitAccess.created(team: team, unit: g.unit, access_mode: read)
                else:
                    if g.access_mode in {read, write}:
                        TeamUnitAccess.created(team: team, unit: g.unit, access_mode: g.access_mode)
                    if g.access_mode in {admin, owner}:
                        TeamUnitAccess.created(team: team, unit: g.unit, access_mode: write)
        if includes_all_repositories:
            for r in repositories/Repositories where r.owner_org = org:
                TeamRepository.created(team: team, repository: r)
        TeamCreated(team: team, actor: actor)

    @guidance
        -- Web: GET/POST /org/{org}/teams/new. API: POST /orgs/{org}/teams
        -- (units_map: unit key -> none|read|write|admin).
        -- Normalisation: an admin team gets admin on every unit and read on
        -- external wiki/tracker; a read/write team keeps its per-unit
        -- choices clamped to write, external units to read, and its
        -- summary access_mode is the lowest non-none unit grant.
}

-- Editing any team except Owners.
-- from: routers/web/org/teams.go:530
rule OwnerEditsTeam {
    when: OwnerEditsTeam(actor, team, name, description, access_mode, grants, includes_all_repositories, can_create_org_repo)

    requires: is_org_owner(team.organization, actor) or actor.is_admin
    requires: not team.is_owners_team
    requires: is_alpha_dash_dot(name)
    requires: length(name) <= config.max_team_name_length
    requires: lower(name) != "new"
    requires: not team_name_taken_by_other(team, name)
    requires: description = null or length(description) <= config.max_team_description_length
    requires: access_mode in {read, write, admin}
    requires: access_mode = admin or grants_some_unit(grants)

    let effective_mode = team_mode_for(access_mode, grants)
    let was_includes_all = team.includes_all_repositories

    ensures: team.name = name
    ensures: team.description = description
    ensures: team.access_mode = effective_mode
    ensures: team.includes_all_repositories = includes_all_repositories
    ensures: team.can_create_org_repo = can_create_org_repo
    ensures:
        for old in team.unit_accesses:
            not exists old
        if access_mode = admin:
            -- every unit at admin; the external wiki and tracker at read
            TeamUnitAccess.created(team: team, unit: code, access_mode: admin)
            TeamUnitAccess.created(team: team, unit: issues, access_mode: admin)
            TeamUnitAccess.created(team: team, unit: pull_requests, access_mode: admin)
            TeamUnitAccess.created(team: team, unit: releases, access_mode: admin)
            TeamUnitAccess.created(team: team, unit: wiki, access_mode: admin)
            TeamUnitAccess.created(team: team, unit: external_wiki, access_mode: read)
            TeamUnitAccess.created(team: team, unit: external_tracker, access_mode: read)
            TeamUnitAccess.created(team: team, unit: projects, access_mode: admin)
            TeamUnitAccess.created(team: team, unit: packages, access_mode: admin)
            TeamUnitAccess.created(team: team, unit: actions, access_mode: admin)
        else:
            for g in grants:
                if g.unit in {external_wiki, external_tracker}:
                    if g.access_mode != none:
                        TeamUnitAccess.created(team: team, unit: g.unit, access_mode: read)
                else:
                    if g.access_mode in {read, write}:
                        TeamUnitAccess.created(team: team, unit: g.unit, access_mode: g.access_mode)
                    if g.access_mode in {admin, owner}:
                        TeamUnitAccess.created(team: team, unit: g.unit, access_mode: write)
    ensures:
        if includes_all_repositories and not was_includes_all:
            for r in repositories/Repositories where r.owner_org = team.organization:
                if not team_covers(team, r):
                    TeamRepository.created(team: team, repository: r)
    ensures: TeamUpdated(team: team, actor: actor)
    ensures: TeamAccessChanged(team: team)

    @guidance
        -- Web: GET/POST /org/{org}/teams/{team}/edit. API: PATCH
        -- /teams/{id} (all fields optional). Any edit of mode, unit grants or
        -- includes-all is an access change for access.allium. Switching
        -- includes-all off keeps the repositories already linked.
}

-- The Owners team keeps its name, owner access, all repositories and the
-- right to create repositories; only its description can change.
-- from: routers/web/org/teams.go:567
rule OwnerEditsOwnersTeamDescription {
    when: OwnerEditsOwnersTeamDescription(actor, team, description)

    requires: is_org_owner(team.organization, actor) or actor.is_admin
    requires: team.is_owners_team
    requires: description = null or length(description) <= config.max_team_description_length

    ensures: team.description = description
    ensures: TeamUpdated(team: team, actor: actor)
}

-- from: models/org_team.go:323
rule OwnerDeletesTeam {
    when: OwnerDeletesTeam(actor, team)

    requires: is_org_owner(team.organization, actor) or actor.is_admin
    requires: not team.is_owners_team

    ensures:
        for i in team.invites:
            not exists i
        for tu in team.unit_accesses:
            not exists tu
        for tr in team.repository_links:
            not exists tr
        for tm in team.memberships:
            not exists tm
            TeamMemberRemoved(team: team, user: tm.user)
        not exists team
        TeamDeleted(team: team)

    @guidance
        -- Web: POST /org/{org}/teams/{team}/delete. API: DELETE /teams/{id}.
        -- code removes the team from branch-protection allow lists and
        -- pulls drops review requests addressed to it (both react to
        -- TeamDeleted). Members left without any team leave the org.
}

------------------------------------------------------------
-- Rules: team membership
------------------------------------------------------------

-- An owner puts a person on a team. With ADD_MEMBERS_BY_INVITATIONS and a
-- person who is not yet an org member (and is not the owner themself), an
-- invitation is sent instead so the person consents to joining.
-- from: services/org/team_invite.go:34
rule OwnerAddsTeamMember {
    when: OwnerAddsTeamMember(actor, team, user)

    requires: is_org_owner(team.organization, actor) or actor.is_admin
    requires: user.kind in {individual, bot, remote}
    requires: not is_team_member(team, user)
    requires: not has_pending_team_invite(team, user)

    let org = team.organization
    let needs_consent = config.add_members_by_invitations and actor != user and not is_org_member(org, user)

    ensures:
        if needs_consent:
            let invite = TeamInvite.created(
                team: team,
                organization: org,
                inviter: actor,
                email: user.primary_email,
                invited_user: user,
                token: new_invite_token(),
                created_at: now,
                expires_at: if config.team_invitation_expiry > 0.days: now + config.team_invitation_expiry else: null,
                status: pending
            )
            TeamInviteCreated(invite: invite, inviter: actor)
        else:
            if not is_org_member(org, user):
                OrgMembership.created(
                    organization: org,
                    user: user,
                    is_public: config.default_org_member_visible,
                    joined_at: now
                )
                OrgMemberAdded(organization: org, user: user)
            TeamMembership.created(
                team: team,
                organization: org,
                user: user,
                reason: added_by_user,
                added_by: actor,
                added_at: now
            )
            TeamMemberAdded(team: team, user: user)

    @guidance
        -- Web: POST /org/{org}/teams/{team}/action/add (uname). API: PUT
        -- /teams/{id}/members/{username}. An expired invitation for the same
        -- person is replaced. repositories reacts to TeamMemberAdded by
        -- auto-watching the team's repositories when AUTO_WATCH_NEW_REPOS.
}

-- An owner invites an e-mail address that has no account (yet).
-- from: models/organization/team_invite.go:112
rule OwnerInvitesEmailToTeam {
    when: OwnerInvitesEmailToTeam(actor, team, email)

    requires: is_org_owner(team.organization, actor) or actor.is_admin
    requires: mail_service_enabled()
    requires: is_valid_email(email)
    requires: not has_pending_team_invite_for_email(team, email)
    requires: not has_member_with_email(team, email)

    ensures:
        let invite = TeamInvite.created(
            team: team,
            organization: team.organization,
            inviter: actor,
            email: email,
            invited_user: null,
            token: new_invite_token(),
            created_at: now,
            expires_at: if config.team_invitation_expiry > 0.days: now + config.team_invitation_expiry else: null,
            status: pending
        )
        TeamInviteCreated(invite: invite, inviter: actor)

    @guidance
        -- Web: the same "add" box on the team page, when the text is an
        -- e-mail address and no account has that name.
}

-- An owner places themself on a team.
-- from: routers/web/org/teams.go:81
rule OwnerJoinsTeam {
    when: OwnerJoinsTeam(actor, team)

    requires: is_org_owner(team.organization, actor) or actor.is_admin
    requires: not is_team_member(team, actor)

    let org = team.organization

    ensures:
        if not is_org_member(org, actor):
            OrgMembership.created(
                organization: org,
                user: actor,
                is_public: config.default_org_member_visible,
                joined_at: now
            )
            OrgMemberAdded(organization: org, user: actor)
        TeamMembership.created(
            team: team,
            organization: org,
            user: actor,
            reason: added_by_user,
            added_by: actor,
            added_at: now
        )
        TeamMemberAdded(team: team, user: actor)

    @guidance
        -- Web: POST /org/{org}/teams/{team}/action/join.
}

-- A member takes themself off a team.
-- from: routers/web/org/teams.go:87
rule MemberLeavesTeam {
    when: MemberLeavesTeam(user, team)

    let tm = TeamMembership{team: team, user: user}

    requires: exists tm
    requires: not team.is_owners_team or team.member_count > 1

    ensures: not exists tm
    ensures: TeamMemberRemoved(team: team, user: user)

    @guidance
        -- Web: POST /org/{org}/teams/{team}/action/leave.
}

-- from: models/org_team.go:462
rule OwnerRemovesTeamMember {
    when: OwnerRemovesTeamMember(actor, team, user)

    let tm = TeamMembership{team: team, user: user}

    requires: is_org_owner(team.organization, actor) or actor.is_admin
    requires: exists tm
    requires: not team.is_owners_team or team.member_count > 1

    ensures: not exists tm
    ensures: TeamMemberRemoved(team: team, user: user)

    @guidance
        -- Web: POST /org/{org}/teams/{team}/action/remove?uid=.
        -- API: DELETE /teams/{id}/members/{username}.
}

-- At sign-in (and on the scheduled LDAP sync) an authentication source asserts
-- the person's external groups; its group-to-team map (static
-- {group: {org: [team]}} or dynamic patterns capturing {org} and {team})
-- says which teams that means.
-- from: services/auth/source/source_group_sync.go:29
rule SyncTeamsFromExternalGroups {
    when: authentication/ExternalGroupsAsserted(user, source, groups)

    ensures:
        for team in teams_mapped_from(source, groups):
            if not is_team_member(team, user):
                AuthSourceSyncAddsTeamMember(source, user, team)
        for team in teams_unmapped_from(source, user, groups):
            AuthSourceSyncRemovesTeamMember(source, user, team)

    @guidance
        -- teams_unmapped_from is empty unless the source removes memberships
        -- for groups the person no longer has (group_team_map_removal).
        -- Teams or organizations named in the map that do not exist are
        -- skipped.
}

-- When an authentication source is deleted, memberships it created stay but
-- lose their provenance.
-- from: models/organization/team_user.go:48
rule ForgetDeletedAuthSourceProvenance {
    when: authentication/AuthSourceDeleted(source)

    ensures:
        for tm in TeamMemberships where auth_source = source:
            tm.auth_source = null
}

-- An authentication source (LDAP group, OAuth2 group claim) maps a group the
-- person belongs to onto a team.
-- from: services/auth/source/source_group_sync.go:332
rule AuthSourceSyncAddsTeamMember {
    when: AuthSourceSyncAddsTeamMember(source, user, team)

    requires: not is_team_member(team, user)

    let org = team.organization

    ensures:
        if not is_org_member(org, user):
            OrgMembership.created(
                organization: org,
                user: user,
                is_public: config.default_org_member_visible,
                joined_at: now
            )
            OrgMemberAdded(organization: org, user: user)
        TeamMembership.created(
            team: team,
            organization: org,
            user: user,
            reason: added_by_auth_source,
            auth_source: source,
            added_at: now
        )
        TeamMemberAdded(team: team, user: user)

    @guidance
        -- No invitation: the identity provider's group membership is the consent.
}

-- from: services/auth/source/source_group_sync.go:231
rule AuthSourceSyncRemovesTeamMember {
    when: AuthSourceSyncRemovesTeamMember(source, user, team)

    let tm = TeamMembership{team: team, user: user}

    requires: exists tm
    requires: not team.is_owners_team or team.member_count > 1

    ensures: not exists tm
    ensures: TeamMemberRemoved(team: team, user: user)

    @guidance
        -- Only when the source is configured to remove memberships for groups
        -- the person has left. The last owner is skipped, not an error.
}

------------------------------------------------------------
-- Rules: team invitations
------------------------------------------------------------

-- from: services/org/team_invite.go:50
rule InviteeAcceptsTeamInvite {
    when: InviteeAcceptsTeamInvite(user, invite, hide_membership)

    requires: invite.status = pending
    requires: (invite.invited_user = null or invite.invited_user = user)
    requires: not is_team_member(invite.team, user)

    let team = invite.team
    let org = invite.organization
    let membership = OrgMembership{organization: org, user: user}

    ensures:
        if exists membership:
            membership.is_public = not hide_membership
        else:
            OrgMembership.created(
                organization: org,
                user: user,
                is_public: not hide_membership,
                joined_at: now
            )
            OrgMemberAdded(organization: org, user: user)
        TeamMembership.created(
            team: team,
            organization: org,
            user: user,
            reason: added_by_user,
            added_by: invite.inviter,
            added_at: now
        )
        TeamMemberAdded(team: team, user: user)
        not exists invite

    @guidance
        -- Web: GET/POST /org/invite/{token} (anyone signed in holding the link
        -- of an e-mail invitation; only the named person for an account
        -- invitation). API: POST /user/team_invitations/{id}/accept
        -- (hide_membership). After accepting, the next pending invitation
        -- into the same org, if any, is shown.
}

-- from: services/org/team_invite.go:76
rule InviteeDeclinesTeamInvite {
    when: InviteeDeclinesTeamInvite(user, invite)

    requires: invite.status = pending
    requires: (invite.invited_user = null or invite.invited_user = user)

    ensures: not exists invite
    ensures: TeamInviteDeclined(invite: invite)

    @guidance
        -- Web: POST /org/invite/{token}/decline.
        -- API: POST /user/team_invitations/{id}/decline.
}

-- from: models/organization/team_invite.go:247
rule OwnerRevokesTeamInvite {
    when: OwnerRevokesTeamInvite(actor, team, invite)

    requires: invite.team = team
    requires: is_org_owner(invite.organization, actor) or actor.is_admin

    ensures: not exists invite

    @guidance
        -- Web: POST /org/{org}/teams/{team}/action/remove_invite?iid=.
        -- API: DELETE /teams/{id}/invitations/{inviteid}. Works on pending
        -- and expired invitations alike.
}

-- An invitation stops being usable once its expiry passes. It stays listed
-- (as expired) until revoked or replaced by a new invitation.
-- from: models/organization/team_invite.go:405
rule TeamInviteExpires {
    when: invite: TeamInvite.expires_at <= now

    requires: invite.status = pending

    ensures: invite.status = expired
}

------------------------------------------------------------
-- Rules: team repositories
------------------------------------------------------------

-- from: services/org/repo.go:16
rule OwnerAddsRepositoryToTeam {
    when: OwnerAddsRepositoryToTeam(actor, team, repository)

    requires: is_org_owner(team.organization, actor) or actor.is_admin
    requires: repository.owner_org = team.organization
    requires: not team_covers(team, repository)

    ensures: TeamRepository.created(team: team, repository: repository)
    ensures: TeamRepositoryAdded(team: team, repository: repository)

    @guidance
        -- Web: POST /org/{org}/teams/{team}/action/repo/add (repo_name).
        -- API: PUT /teams/{id}/repos/{org}/{repo} (owner of the org, or
        -- admin of the repository — see RepoAdminAddsTeamToRepository).
}

-- from: routers/web/repo/setting/collaboration.go:152
rule RepoAdminAddsTeamToRepository {
    when: RepoAdminAddsTeamToRepository(actor, repository, team)

    requires: is_repo_admin(actor, repository) or actor.is_admin
    requires: repository.owner_org = team.organization
    requires: team.organization.repo_admin_change_team_access
        or is_org_owner(team.organization, actor) or actor.is_admin
    requires: not team_covers(team, repository)

    ensures: TeamRepository.created(team: team, repository: repository)
    ensures: TeamRepositoryAdded(team: team, repository: repository)

    @guidance
        -- Web: POST /{owner}/{repo}/settings/collaboration/team.
        -- API: PUT /repos/{owner}/{repo}/teams/{team}.
}

-- Removing a repository from a team that includes all repositories is a no-op.
-- from: services/repository/delete.go:477
rule OwnerRemovesRepositoryFromTeam {
    when: OwnerRemovesRepositoryFromTeam(actor, team, repository)

    let link = TeamRepository{team: team, repository: repository}

    requires: is_org_owner(team.organization, actor) or actor.is_admin
    requires: exists link
    requires: not team.includes_all_repositories

    ensures: not exists link
    ensures: TeamRepositoryRemoved(team: team, repository: repository)

    @guidance
        -- Web: POST /org/{org}/teams/{team}/action/repo/remove (repoid).
        -- API: DELETE /teams/{id}/repos/{org}/{repo}. Members who lose read
        -- access stop watching the repository and its issues (repositories
        -- and issues react to TeamRepositoryRemoved).
}

-- from: routers/web/repo/setting/collaboration.go:198
rule RepoAdminRemovesTeamFromRepository {
    when: RepoAdminRemovesTeamFromRepository(actor, repository, team)

    let link = TeamRepository{team: team, repository: repository}

    requires: is_repo_admin(actor, repository) or actor.is_admin
    requires: team.organization.repo_admin_change_team_access
        or is_org_owner(team.organization, actor) or actor.is_admin
    requires: exists link
    requires: not team.includes_all_repositories

    ensures: not exists link
    ensures: TeamRepositoryRemoved(team: team, repository: repository)

    @guidance
        -- Web: POST /{owner}/{repo}/settings/collaboration/team/delete.
        -- API: DELETE /repos/{owner}/{repo}/teams/{team}.
}

-- from: models/org_team.go:63
rule OwnerAddsAllRepositoriesToTeam {
    when: OwnerAddsAllRepositoriesToTeam(actor, team)

    requires: is_org_owner(team.organization, actor) or actor.is_admin

    ensures:
        for r in repositories/Repositories where r.owner_org = team.organization:
            if not team_covers(team, r):
                TeamRepository.created(team: team, repository: r)
                TeamRepositoryAdded(team: team, repository: r)

    @guidance
        -- Web: POST /org/{org}/teams/{team}/action/repo/addall. A one-off
        -- copy; future repositories are only added when includes-all is on.
}

-- from: models/org_team.go:79
rule OwnerRemovesAllRepositoriesFromTeam {
    when: OwnerRemovesAllRepositoriesFromTeam(actor, team)

    requires: is_org_owner(team.organization, actor) or actor.is_admin
    requires: not team.includes_all_repositories

    ensures:
        for tr in team.repository_links:
            not exists tr
            TeamRepositoryRemoved(team: team, repository: tr.repository)

    @guidance
        -- Web: POST /org/{org}/teams/{team}/action/repo/removeall.
}

-- A new repository in the org joins every includes-all team.
-- from: modules/repository/create.go:126
rule IncludeNewRepositoryInAllRepoTeams {
    when: repository: repositories/Repository.created

    requires: repository.owner_org != null

    ensures:
        for t in repository.owner_org.teams where includes_all_repositories = true:
            TeamRepository.created(team: t, repository: repository)
            TeamRepositoryAdded(team: t, repository: repository)

    @guidance
        -- repositories also makes the creator a repository admin
        -- collaborator when no team already gives them admin.
}

-- A repository transferred into the org joins every includes-all team.
-- from: services/repository/transfer.go:186
rule IncludeTransferredRepositoryInAllRepoTeams {
    when: OrgRepositoryArrived(repository)

    requires: repository.owner_org != null

    ensures:
        for t in repository.owner_org.teams where includes_all_repositories = true:
            if not team_covers(t, repository):
                TeamRepository.created(team: t, repository: repository)
                TeamRepositoryAdded(team: t, repository: repository)
}

-- A repository that leaves the org (transfer out, deletion) leaves every team.
-- from: models/organization/org.go:612
rule DropTeamLinksOfDepartedRepository {
    when: OrgRepositoryDeparted(repository, org)

    ensures:
        for t in org.teams:
            for tr in t.repository_links where repository = repository:
                not exists tr
                TeamRepositoryRemoved(team: t, repository: repository)
}

------------------------------------------------------------
-- Invariants
------------------------------------------------------------

-- Every organization has exactly one Owners team.
invariant OneOwnersTeamPerOrganization {
    for org in Organizations:
        (org.teams where is_owners_team = true).count = 1
}

-- The Owners team is never empty: an organization always has an owner.
invariant OrganizationAlwaysHasAnOwner {
    for org in Organizations:
        org.owner_count >= 1
}

-- The Owners team has owner access over every repository and may create repos.
invariant OwnersTeamShape {
    for t in Teams where is_owners_team = true:
        t.access_mode = owner and t.includes_all_repositories and t.can_create_org_repo
}

-- Only the Owners team carries owner access.
invariant OnlyOwnersTeamHasOwnerMode {
    for t in Teams:
        t.access_mode = owner implies t.is_owners_team
}

-- A team never grants "none" overall.
invariant TeamGrantsSomething {
    for t in Teams:
        t.access_mode != none
}

-- Team names are unique within an organization, ignoring case.
invariant TeamNamesUniquePerOrganization {
    for t in Teams:
        t.organization.teams.all(o => o = t or lower(o.name) != lower(t.name))
}

-- A person is an org member exactly when they are on at least one of its teams.
invariant MembershipIsTeamMembership {
    for m in OrgMemberships:
        m.team_memberships.count >= 1
}

invariant TeamMembersAreOrgMembers {
    for tm in TeamMemberships:
        exists OrgMembership{organization: tm.team.organization, user: tm.user}
}

invariant TeamMembershipOrganizationMatches {
    for tm in TeamMemberships:
        tm.organization = tm.team.organization
}

-- Only people (not organizations) are members; organizations are separate entities.
invariant MembersArePeople {
    for m in OrgMemberships:
        m.user.kind in {individual, bot, remote}
}

-- A team only covers repositories its organization owns.
invariant TeamRepositoriesBelongToOrganization {
    for tr in TeamRepositories:
        tr.repository.owner_org = tr.team.organization
}

-- An includes-all team covers every repository of its organization.
invariant IncludesAllMeansAll {
    for t in Teams where includes_all_repositories = true:
        for r in repositories/Repositories where r.owner_org = t.organization:
            r in t.repositories
}

-- External wiki and tracker units can at most be read.
invariant ExternalUnitsReadOnly {
    for tu in TeamUnitAccesses:
        tu.unit in {external_wiki, external_tracker} implies tu.access_mode in {none, read}
}

-- Read/write teams grant at most write on any unit.
invariant NonAdminTeamsCapUnitsAtWrite {
    for tu in TeamUnitAccesses:
        tu.team.access_mode in {read, write} implies tu.access_mode in {none, read, write}
}

-- At most one pending invitation per team and address.
invariant OnePendingInvitePerAddress {
    for i in TeamInvites where status = pending:
        i.team.pending_invites.all(o => o = i or o.email != i.email)
}

invariant InviteOrganizationMatches {
    for i in TeamInvites:
        i.organization = i.team.organization
}

-- Account invitations carry the invited person's address.
invariant AccountInviteAddressed {
    for i in TeamInvites:
        i.invited_user != null implies i.email != ""
}

------------------------------------------------------------
-- Actor Declarations
------------------------------------------------------------

-- Signed-in users, site administrators and anonymous visitors are the shared
-- actors access/SignedInUser, access/SiteAdmin and access/Visitor.

-- A member of the Owners team (site admins act as owners everywhere).
actor OrgOwner {
    within: Organization
    identified_by: accounts/User where is_org_owner(within, this) or is_admin = true
}

-- Anybody on at least one of the organization's teams.
actor OrgMember {
    within: Organization
    identified_by: accounts/User where is_org_member(within, this) or is_admin = true
}

-- An owner of the organization a team belongs to (or a site admin), managing
-- that team.
actor TeamOwner {
    within: Team
    identified_by: accounts/User where is_org_owner(within.organization, this) or is_admin = true
}

-- Somebody allowed to open a given team's page.
actor TeamViewer {
    within: Team
    identified_by: accounts/User where can_view_team(within, this) or is_admin = true
}

-- An admin of a repository owned by an organization is access/RepoAdmin.

------------------------------------------------------------
-- Surfaces
------------------------------------------------------------

-- Founding an organization.
surface OrganizationCreation {
    facing user: access/SignedInUser

    exposes:
        config.default_org_visibility
        user.allow_create_organization
        config.disable_regular_org_creation

    provides:
        UserCreatesOrganization(user, name, visibility, repo_admin_change_team_access)
            when user.is_admin or (user.allow_create_organization and not config.disable_regular_org_creation)

    @guidance
        -- Web: GET/POST /org/create. API: POST /orgs. The "New organization"
        -- entry is hidden when the person may not create one.
}

-- The org profile as an anonymous visitor sees it: public orgs only, public
-- members only, no teams.
surface AnonymousOrganizationProfile {
    facing visitor: access/Visitor

    context org: Organization where visibility = public

    exposes:
        org.name
        org.full_name
        org.description
        org.website
        org.location
        org.visibility
        for m in org.memberships where is_public:
            m.user.name

    @guidance
        -- Web: GET /{org} (home, repositories, .profile README), GET
        -- /org/{org}/members. API: GET /orgs/{org} (e-mail withheld from
        -- anonymous callers), GET /orgs/{org}/public_members,
        -- GET /orgs/{org}/public_members/{username}. Limited and private orgs
        -- are not found for anonymous visitors.
        -- Profile README: if the org owns a non-fork, public, non-empty
        -- repository named ".profile" that the viewer can read, its README
        -- from the default branch is rendered on the home page, and its
        -- FUNDING file (if any) is shown.
}

-- The org profile as any signed-in person who may see the org sees it.
surface OrganizationProfile {
    facing viewer: access/SignedInUser

    context org: Organization

    exposes:
        org.name
        org.full_name
        org.description
        org.website
        org.location
        org.email
        org.visibility
        org.member_count when sees_concealed_members(org, viewer)
        for m in org.memberships where is_public or sees_concealed_members(org, viewer):
            m.user.name
        is_org_owner(org, viewer)
        is_org_member(org, viewer)
        can_create_repository_in(viewer, org)

    provides:
        MemberLeavesOrganization(viewer, org)
            when is_org_member(org, viewer) and (not is_org_owner(org, viewer) or owner_count(org) > 1)

    related:
        OrganizationMembersArea(org) when is_org_member(org, viewer)
        OrganizationSettings(org) when is_org_owner(org, viewer)

    @guarantee HiddenFromStrangers
        -- A private organization, or any organization when the viewer is a
        -- restricted user, is not found unless the viewer is a member or a
        -- site admin (is_visible_to). Limited organizations are visible to
        -- every signed-in non-restricted person.

    @guarantee ConcealedMembersStayConcealed
        -- People who are neither members nor site admins only ever see
        -- public memberships, in lists, counts and membership checks.

    @guidance
        -- Web: GET /{org}, GET /org/{org}/members. API: GET /orgs/{org},
        -- GET /orgs (all visible orgs), GET /users/{username}/orgs (public
        -- memberships unless self/admin), GET /user/orgs,
        -- GET /users/{username}/orgs/{org}/permissions (is_owner, is_admin,
        -- can_write, can_read, can_create_repository),
        -- GET /orgs/{org}/members, GET /orgs/{org}/members/{username}
        -- (non-members are redirected to the public_members check).
        -- The members/teams tabs show when the viewer is a member or the
        -- org has public members.
}

-- What members (not only owners) can see and do.
surface OrganizationMembersArea {
    facing member: OrgMember

    context org: Organization

    exposes:
        for m in org.memberships:
            m.user.name
            m.is_public
            is_org_owner(org, m.user)
        for t in org.teams:
            t.name
            t.description
            t.access_mode
            t.member_count
            t.repository_count
            is_team_member(t, member)
        for i in org.invites:
            i.team.name when i.invited_user = member

    provides:
        MemberChangesMembershipVisibility(member, org, membership, is_public)
            when membership.organization = org and (membership.user = member or is_org_owner(org, member))
        MemberLeavesOrganization(member, org)
            when not is_org_owner(org, member) or owner_count(org) > 1

    related:
        TeamPage(t) when can_view_team(t, member)

    @guidance
        -- Web: GET /org/{org}/teams, GET /org/{org}/members (all members with
        -- their 2FA status, owner badge and public/private flag).
        -- API: GET /orgs/{org}/teams, GET /orgs/{org}/teams/search
        -- (non-admins search only their own teams), PUT/DELETE
        -- /orgs/{org}/public_members/{username}.
}

-- A single team's page.
surface TeamPage {
    facing viewer: TeamViewer

    context team: Team

    exposes:
        team.name
        team.description
        team.access_mode
        team.includes_all_repositories
        team.can_create_org_repo
        for u in team.unit_accesses:
            u.unit
            u.access_mode
        for m in team.memberships:
            m.user.name
            m.reason
            m.added_by
            m.added_at
        for r in team.repositories:
            r.name
        for i in team.pending_invites:
            i.email when is_org_owner(team.organization, viewer)
        for i in team.expired_invites:
            i.email when is_org_owner(team.organization, viewer)

    provides:
        MemberLeavesTeam(viewer, team)
            when is_team_member(team, viewer) and (not team.is_owners_team or team.member_count > 1)
        OwnerJoinsTeam(viewer, team)
            when is_org_owner(team.organization, viewer) and not is_team_member(team, viewer)

    @guidance
        -- Web: GET /org/{org}/teams/{team}, GET /org/{org}/teams/{team}/repositories.
        -- API: GET /teams/{id}, GET /teams/{id}/members[/{username}],
        -- GET /teams/{id}/repos[/{org}/{repo}], GET /teams/{id}/invitations,
        -- GET /user/teams. Repositories listed are further limited by the
        -- caller's token scope. A member of the org who is not on the team
        -- (and does not see all teams) is refused; anyone else is not told
        -- the team exists.
}

-- Everything only owners (and site admins) do.
surface OrganizationSettings {
    facing owner: OrgOwner

    context org: Organization

    exposes:
        org.name
        org.full_name
        org.description
        org.website
        org.location
        org.email
        org.visibility
        org.repo_admin_change_team_access
        org.max_repo_creation
        org.has_custom_avatar
        for t in org.teams:
            t.name
        for i in org.invites:
            i.email
            i.status
            i.expires_at

    provides:
        OwnerUpdatesOrganizationProfile(owner, org, full_name, description, website, location, email)
        OwnerChangesOrganizationVisibility(owner, org, visibility)
        OwnerSetsRepoAdminTeamAccess(owner, org, allowed)
        OwnerRenamesOrganization(owner, org, new_name)
        OwnerUploadsOrganizationAvatar(owner, org, image)
        OwnerDeletesOrganizationAvatar(owner, org)
            when org.has_custom_avatar
        OwnerDeletesOrganization(owner, org, confirmation_name)
        OwnerCreatesTeam(owner, org, name, description, access_mode, grants, includes_all_repositories, can_create_org_repo)
        OwnerAddsMemberToOrganization(owner, org, user, teams)
        OwnerRemovesOrgMember(owner, org, user)

    related:
        TeamSettings(t) when t.organization = org

    @guarantee LastOwnerStays
        -- No operation leaves the Owners team empty: removing, leaving or
        -- syncing away the only owner is refused.

    @guarantee OwnersTeamIsPermanent
        -- The Owners team cannot be deleted, renamed, narrowed below owner
        -- access, or detached from any repository.

    @guarantee DeleteNeedsEmptyOrganization
        -- An organization that still owns repositories or packages cannot be
        -- deleted by its owners.

    @guidance
        -- Web: /org/{org}/settings (options, avatar, delete,
        -- blocked_users), /org/{org}/teams/new, /org/{org}/members/action/{add,remove}.
        -- API: PATCH/DELETE /orgs/{org}, POST /orgs/{org}/rename,
        -- POST/DELETE /orgs/{org}/avatar, DELETE /orgs/{org}/members/{username},
        -- POST /orgs/{org}/teams.
        -- Managing one team is TeamSettings.
        -- Settings sub-pages for blocked users (accounts), webhooks, labels,
        -- actions, packages, OAuth2 applications and storage overview belong
        -- to their own modules.
        -- A non-owner member gets "forbidden"; a non-member gets "not found".
}

-- Managing one team: only owners of its organization (and site admins).
surface TeamSettings {
    facing owner: TeamOwner

    context team: Team

    exposes:
        team.name
        team.description
        team.access_mode
        team.includes_all_repositories
        team.can_create_org_repo
        for i in team.pending_invites:
            i.email
            i.expires_at
        for i in team.expired_invites:
            i.email
            i.expires_at

    provides:
        OwnerEditsTeam(owner, team, name, description, access_mode, grants, includes_all_repositories, can_create_org_repo)
            when not team.is_owners_team
        OwnerEditsOwnersTeamDescription(owner, team, description)
            when team.is_owners_team
        OwnerDeletesTeam(owner, team)
            when not team.is_owners_team
        OwnerAddsTeamMember(owner, team, user)
        OwnerInvitesEmailToTeam(owner, team, email)
            when mail_service_enabled()
        OwnerRemovesTeamMember(owner, team, user)
        OwnerRevokesTeamInvite(owner, team, invite)
            when invite.team = team
        OwnerAddsRepositoryToTeam(owner, team, repository)
        OwnerRemovesRepositoryFromTeam(owner, team, repository)
            when not team.includes_all_repositories
        OwnerAddsAllRepositoriesToTeam(owner, team)
        OwnerRemovesAllRepositoriesFromTeam(owner, team)
            when not team.includes_all_repositories

    @guarantee OwnersTeamIsPermanent
        -- The Owners team cannot be deleted, renamed, narrowed below owner
        -- access, or detached from any repository.

    @guidance
        -- Web: /org/{org}/teams/{team}/edit, /org/{org}/teams/{team}/delete,
        -- /org/{org}/teams/{team}/action/{add,remove,remove_invite},
        -- /org/{org}/teams/{team}/action/repo/{add,remove,addall,removeall}.
        -- API: PATCH/DELETE /teams/{id}, PUT/DELETE /teams/{id}/members/{username},
        -- GET/DELETE /teams/{id}/invitations/{inviteid},
        -- PUT/DELETE /teams/{id}/repos/{org}/{repo}.
        -- A non-owner member gets "forbidden"; a non-member gets "not found".
}

-- Accepting or declining an invitation.
surface TeamInvitation {
    facing invitee: access/SignedInUser

    context invite: TeamInvite where status = pending

    exposes:
        invite.team.name
        invite.organization.name
        invite.inviter.name
        invite.email
        invite.expires_at

    provides:
        InviteeAcceptsTeamInvite(invitee, invite, hide_membership)
            when (invite.invited_user = null or invite.invited_user = invitee)
        InviteeDeclinesTeamInvite(invitee, invite)
            when (invite.invited_user = null or invite.invited_user = invitee)

    timeout:
        TeamInviteExpires

    @guarantee InviteIsPersonal
        -- An invitation addressed to an account can only be seen, accepted
        -- or declined by that account; everyone else is told it does not
        -- exist. An expired invitation is not found.

    @guidance
        -- Web: GET/POST /org/invite/{token}, POST /org/invite/{token}/decline;
        -- the org home page shows a banner for pending invitations into that
        -- org. API: GET /user/team_invitations, GET
        -- /user/team_invitations/{id}, POST .../accept, POST .../decline.
}

-- Team access managed from the repository side.
surface RepositoryTeamAccess {
    facing admin: access/RepoAdmin

    context repository: repositories/Repository where owner_org != null

    exposes:
        repository.owner_org.repo_admin_change_team_access
        for t in repository.owner_org.teams:
            t.name when team_covers(t, repository)
            t.access_mode when team_covers(t, repository)

    provides:
        RepoAdminAddsTeamToRepository(admin, repository, team)
            when repository.owner_org.repo_admin_change_team_access or is_org_owner(repository.owner_org, admin)
        RepoAdminRemovesTeamFromRepository(admin, repository, team)
            when repository.owner_org.repo_admin_change_team_access or is_org_owner(repository.owner_org, admin)

    @guidance
        -- Web: /{owner}/{repo}/settings/collaboration (team section).
        -- API: GET/PUT/DELETE /repos/{owner}/{repo}/teams[/{team}].
}

-- Site administration of organizations.
surface OrganizationAdministration {
    facing admin: access/SiteAdmin

    context org: Organization

    exposes:
        org.name
        org.visibility
        org.member_count
        org.team_count
        org.max_repo_creation

    provides:
        AdminSetsOrganizationRepoLimit(admin, org, limit)

    @guidance
        -- Web: GET /admin/orgs (list all, including private). API: GET
        -- /admin/orgs. Creating an org for a user (POST /admin/users/{username}/orgs)
        -- enters through administration/AdminUserAccount. Site admins also
        -- pass every owner check on OrganizationSettings.
}

------------------------------------------------------------
-- Deferred Specifications
------------------------------------------------------------

deferred Organization.unit_permission    -- see: access.allium (org-level read of projects/packages/code from team units or visibility)

------------------------------------------------------------
-- Open Questions
------------------------------------------------------------

open question "Forgejo's API lets an owner rename the Owners team (PATCH /teams/{id} with a name), which breaks owner detection by name; the web UI does not. This spec forbids it — confirm."
open question "Forgejo does not refuse deleting the Owners team in the backend (only the UI hides the button). This spec refuses it — confirm."
open question "Membership visibility: the web lets owners publicize/conceal other members, the API only lets members change their own. Which should a rebuild keep? (Spec: self or owner.)"
open question "A read/write team's summary access_mode is the lowest non-none unit grant (team_mode_for). Is a summary needed at all, or should read/write teams be defined purely by their unit grants?"
open question "AdminCreatesOrganizationForUser checks the target owner's permission to create organizations rather than the admin's. Intended?"
open question "Team-repository add via API requires repository admin (reqAdmin) plus team membership, while the web requires org ownership. Spec treats the API path as the repo-side RepoAdminAddsTeamToRepository (honouring repo_admin_change_team_access). Confirm."
open question "Should a user block at org level prevent the blocked user from being added to or invited into the org's teams? Forgejo does not check."
open question "Expired invitations are never cleaned up automatically; they stay listed until revoked or replaced. Should a rebuild purge them after some time?"

-- Black-box functions used above (implementation-defined, pure).
-- Membership predicates offered to other modules; each equals the derived
-- value named on the right:
--   is_org_owner(org, user)            -- org.has_owner(user)
--   is_org_member(org, user)           -- org.has_member(user)
--   is_team_member(team, user)         -- team.has_member(user)
--   team_covers(team, repository)      -- team.covers(repository)
--   can_view_team(team, user)          -- team.can_be_viewed_by(user)
--   can_create_repository_in(user, org)-- org.lets_create_repo(user)
--   sees_concealed_members(org, user)  -- org.sees_concealed_members(user)
--   organization_visible_to(org, user) -- org.is_visible_to(user); anonymous: org.is_public
--                                      -- (same as access/can_see_organization(viewer, org))
--   owner_count(org)                   -- org.owner_count
--   belongs_to_organizations(user)     -- some OrgMembership{user: user} exists
--   shares_organization(a, b)          -- a and b are members of a common org, or one is that org
--   can_read_unit(user, org, unit) / can_write_unit(user, org, unit)
--                                      -- org-level unit access: the highest grant for `unit`
--                                      -- across the user's teams in org; with no team, read
--                                      -- when org is public, or limited and the user is signed in
--                                      -- (same as access/organization_unit_mode)
-- Other black boxes:
--   is_repo_admin(user, repository)    -- access/is_repo_admin(user, repository): admin
--                                      -- (or owner) mode on the repository
--   team_name_taken(org, name)         -- some team of org has this name, ignoring case
--   team_name_taken_by_other(team, name)
--   grants_some_unit(grants)           -- at least one grant above none
--   has_pending_team_invite(team, user), has_pending_team_invite_for_email(team, email),
--   has_pending_org_invite(org, user), has_member_with_email(team, email)
--   is_usable_owner_name(name)       -- accounts' user-name rules: charset, reserved names and patterns
--   owner_name_available(name)       -- no user or organization holds this name (ignoring case)
--   owner_name_claimable(name, org)  -- not within accounts' USERNAME_COOLDOWN_PERIOD of another owner's release
--   owned_repository_count(org)      -- repositories with owner_org = org
--   owned_package_count(org)         -- packages owned by org
--   team_mode_for(mode, grants)      -- see OwnerCreatesTeam guidance;
--                                      -- `grants` is a set of {unit: repositories/UnitKind,
--                                      -- access_mode: access/AccessMode} pairs (API units_map)
--   new_invite_token()               -- unguessable, unique
--   mail_service_enabled()           -- [mailer] ENABLED (notifications' outbound mail is configured)
--   is_alpha_dash_dot(s), is_valid_email(s), is_valid_site_url(s), is_acceptable_avatar(img), lower(s), length(s)

------------------------------------------------------------
-- Requests to other modules
------------------------------------------------------------

-- REQUEST accounts/User.allow_create_organization: per-user permission to create orgs (default from [service] DEFAULT_ALLOW_CREATE_ORGANIZATION = true).
-- REQUEST accounts: react to OrganizationRenamed(organization, old_name, new_name) with RenameNamespace semantics (UserRedirect with organization set, MAX_USER_REDIRECTS); react to OrganizationCreated by dropping any redirect holding the new name; follows and blocks of an org removed on OrganizationDeleted.
-- REQUEST accounts: OrganizationBlocksUser should also require that the blocked user is not the acting owner (Forgejo refuses blocking yourself).
-- REQUEST accounts: owner-name namespace — a name may be held by a User or an Organization, never both (is_usable_owner_name, owner_name_available, owner_name_claimable as black boxes over accounts' rules).
-- REQUEST access: derive repository permission for org repositories from TeamRepository + TeamUnitAccess + Team.access_mode (owner/admin teams: all units), and org-level unit read (projects/packages/code) from team units or org visibility.
-- REQUEST repositories: emit OrgRepositoryArrived(repository) after a transfer into an org, and OrgRepositoryDeparted(repository, organization) when an org repository is transferred out or deleted.
-- REQUEST repositories: when an org repository is created and no team gives its creator admin, add the creator as an admin Collaboration; check can_create_repository_in(user, org) and Organization.max_repo_creation for creation, forks, transfers and push-to-create.
-- REQUEST repositories: react to TeamMemberAdded / TeamRepositoryAdded with auto-watch when AUTO_WATCH_NEW_REPOS; react to TeamMemberRemoved / OrgMemberRemoved / TeamRepositoryRemoved by unwatching repositories the user can no longer read; react to OrganizationPurgeStarted by deleting all org repositories.
-- REQUEST issues: react to TeamMemberRemoved / OrgMemberRemoved / TeamRepositoryRemoved by removing IssueWatch and assignments the user can no longer hold.
-- REQUEST packages: react to OrganizationPurgeStarted by deleting all org packages; expose owned package count.
-- REQUEST actions: react to OrganizationDeleted by deleting org secrets, variables, runners and runner registration tokens.
-- REQUEST code: react to TeamDeleted by removing the team from ProtectedBranch / ProtectedTag allow lists.
-- REQUEST pulls: react to TeamDeleted by removing team ReviewRequests.
-- REQUEST notifications: react to TeamInviteCreated by mailing invite.email with the invite link (inviter, org, team).
-- REQUEST authentication: black boxes teams_mapped_from(source, groups) / teams_unmapped_from(source, user, groups) read the source's group_team_map, dynamic maps and group_team_map_removal.
-- REQUEST moderation: ReportableContentChanging is not raised from here yet; the integration pass should decide how org profile edits (OrganizationProfileUpdated, OrganizationRenamed, OrganizationAvatarChanged) feed moderation's shadow copies.
